  "worked_solution": "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $R$ (the old housing complex) and the area of the image $T(R)$ (the new housing complex) under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(R))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(R)\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(R)=16\\,\\text{hectares}.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of the matrix $T$ (found in part 1), we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot (-1)-(2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(R)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(R) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the new housing complex is $48$ hectares.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
